Whitney Hodges: Austin venues right now. We have one in North Texas, we have one in San Antonio, and then, of course, all over the U.S. But there are quite a few venues that we work with in what we call, like, a full-service capacity, right? Which it sounds like is what you would be looking for. You're not necessarily looking to learn how to.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.000
judy: Awesome. Yeah.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.000
judy: Yeah.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.000
judy: Yes.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Whitney Hodges: run the ads yourself, or go into the ad accounts, or anything like that. So, you know, it's a white glove service where we really are setting up everything for you, um, within your Google Ads account, within your Meta Ads account.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.000
judy: Yep.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.000
judy: No.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.000
judy: Right.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, you know, we're taking care of all of the, uh, the copywriting, designing all the ad creatives, you know, formulating the right headlines, really building everything and, um, and launching everything, right?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.000
judy: Yeah.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:27.000
Whitney Hodges: continually managing things. So you know, in on how performance is at least a few times a week, making adjustments as needed, reporting to you, you know, on a monthly basis on how things are looking, getting on a monthly strategy call.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.000
judy: Right.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.000
judy: Okay.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.000
judy: Okay.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, with you as well. So… and the way that I would put it, right, it's not really just that we're running your ads, we're truly building a client acquisition system for you, right?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.000
judy: Right.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.000
judy: Right. Uh-huh.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, the goal is not just to get visibility, that's part of it, right? But we want that visibility to result in more leads, and we want additional leads to result in more tours, which ultimately, of course, results in more bookings.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.000
judy: Right.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.000
judy: Right.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.000
judy: Right, right.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:12.000
Whitney Hodges: for you. So, you know, another piece of that that's typically layered in with our venue clients is our lead management platform. So I'm kind of curious on your end, I think you said that you used HoneyBook.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:27.000
Whitney Hodges: You know, I saw that you kind of have a process in place for when an inquiry comes in, that you're emailing, you're providing a link to kind of book a tour. Um, they're getting back to you if they want to book that tour. I am curious, though, kind of beyond that initial touchpoint.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.000
judy: Right.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.000
judy: Right.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, what else is happening on your end, right? Is there, like, are there email follow-up sequences, or Brittany and the team following up? What does that look like?

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.000
judy: Oh, yes. Okay.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:46.000
judy: So, um, since I kind of told you already, you know, what our process is once we get the lead in.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Alright.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:52.000
judy: Then, uh, you know, they come out for a tour, and we follow up.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:18:03.000
judy: We do a follow-up email with, um, clarifying all the pricing, which isn't that much, because basically we're just a venue rental, but have all this stuff included.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.000
Whitney Hodges: I don't know.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.000
judy: And.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.000
judy: We…

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:12.000
judy: I have an actual… and I can send you, like, our, um…

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:21.000
judy: you know, what we use, so you can see it, because we use the same thing, and just fill in the spots. But we, um…

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:32.000
judy: Follow up with that, and then, like, uh, oh, if you want us to hold a date, we'll hold a date for, you know, 3 days with no cost, and…

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.000
Whitney Hodges: Thank you.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:41.000
judy: Uh, kind of things like that, and then open it up to, you know, if you have any questions, please let us know. Um…

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:46.000
judy: That's kind of where… and then we ended there. You know, like, if they…

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:52.000
judy: Don't book with the… I mean, if they even get back with us, you know, which is…

00:18:52.000 --> 00:19:06.000
judy: hard to get people to get back with you once they're like, no, I don't want that, you know, and that's understandable. And, uh, so we don't really get any feedback after that, you know, yeah.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Mm-hmm. Okay.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.000
judy: And then I would send them.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:23.000
judy: So they're like, oh, hey, yeah, we want a book. So we're like, we'll double check the calendar and we then go, okay, great. And we have another letter we send out and email and then we.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.000
Whitney Hodges: No.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:39.000
judy: uh… oh, then I make sure I have all the information, which isn't much, through HoneyBook to do a contract, and then we send it through HoneyBook, and they can pay for it and pay, um…

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:57.000
judy: online. They can pay online and sign, I mean. And, yeah. And so that's, uh… and then they get reminders through HoneyBook for, you know, when a payment's due, or, you know, different things like that. They can communicate with us through HoneyBook, since I know you're familiar with it.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Thank you.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Great. Yeah.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.000
judy: But, um…

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:13.000
judy: They don't always, and we do ask, we're, uh, I don't know the word I would use, but we try to make sure people communicate with us through HoneyBook or email instead of a phone call.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:19.000
judy: So that we always have a record of what was said, if that makes sense. Yeah.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Okay.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:26.000
judy: and so that kind of… I know that takes some of the personal touch out, but we also will, you know, like, if you want to come out and.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:39.000
judy: you know, do another… not a tour, but a site visit. You know, once you've booked, then that's not a problem. And, you know, one of us will probably be out there and can answer any questions, that type of thing. Yeah.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, got it.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:43.000
judy: So that's kind of where how we do it. Yeah.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, okay, good to know. So, do you find, though, um, that you get a lot of people that will just kind of, like, inquire, like, fill out your general contact form, but then don't necessarily turn into book tours, or…

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.000
judy: Yeah.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:01.000
judy: Uh, oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, I would say…

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.000
Whitney Hodges: No. Okay.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.000
judy: Over 50%.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, okay, got it. Um, and so, you know, if somebody's just kind of, like, inquiring, and you send them that, you know, initial email that has more details, that has the link to book a tour, um…

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.000
judy: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.000
judy: Yeah. Okay.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.000
judy: Right.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:25.000
Whitney Hodges: The… the ball's just kind of in their court at that point to respond back, or are you guys going back and, like, following up with those people, like…

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:32.000
judy: Uh, no, it's kind of in there for them to respond back to us, yeah. Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Got it. Okay. So that potentially could be, you know, a missed opportunity there. What we are seeing just kind of industry-wide as, like, a best practice for venues is typically when somebody inquires.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.000
judy: Yeah.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, sending them the email, just like you are, right, with the additional details, with the link to book a tour, but then from there, putting them in a follow-up sequence.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:51.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.000
judy: Okay.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Whitney Hodges: So, um, you know, some venues will do, you know, a sequence that happens over the course of a week to two weeks. Others, it'll be 30, 60, 90 days, where they have a system in place to continuously be.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:05.000
judy: Oh.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:14.000
judy: Oh, okay.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and, you know, it… that's… that's a lot to keep up with manually, right? So that's not something that I would… would necessarily recommend. Um, but that is where, um, our lead management platform that I was mentioning, LeadLock, really can kind of come into play.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.000
judy: Yeah.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.000
judy: Yes.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.000
judy: Right.

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:44.000
Whitney Hodges: And fill that gap, right? Yeah. So, um, you know, an inquiry comes in, and typically what we will do is that, uh, that email that it sounds like you guys are already sending, we do typically automate that, so that people are receiving that.

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:31.000
judy: I saw y'all had that. Yeah.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:42.000
judy: Thank you.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:56.000
Whitney Hodges: right away, you know, if you're… if you're open to that, because we do find that today's couples, especially Gen Z, they just really want that instant gratification, you know, they want the information when they want it, sort of.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.000
judy: Okay.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.000
judy: Okay.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.000
judy: Right.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.000
judy: Right.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, another part of the system, too, is, uh, is text messaging. So, um, do you guys currently use texting at all as part of the sales process?

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:09.000
judy: No, we don't. Yeah. Yeah.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, okay, yeah. So, for today's generation, that's… that's also what we found is really important to them, like, being able to communicate through text. So, with the… the system, though, what's really nice about it is that it does keep everything.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:35.000
Whitney Hodges: organized, and all in one spot. So, none of you would be using your personal phone numbers, it's all a phone number that goes through the LeadLock system. Um, and it's all…

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.000
judy: Okay.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:30.000
judy: Okay.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:35.000
judy: Oh, last year.

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, can you hear me, Judy?

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.000
judy: Nope.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:42.000
judy: Yeah, yeah. Okay, I can hear you now. I missed it a little bit, but yeah.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, no worries. What did you hear me last day?

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:56.000
judy: Uh, about that the system has everything for us to, you know, be able to view, and you're not, like, losing all the information that they responded with or such, yeah.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:24:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Correct, yeah. So, it's not like the text messaging would be happening on Brittany's phone or anybody else on the team individually, right? It's in a spot where all of you would be able to log in and see any that are happening via text message.

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:58.000
judy: Okay.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.000
judy: No.

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.000
judy: Oh, okay.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.000
judy: Okay.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.000
Whitney Hodges: And so…

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:24.000
Whitney Hodges: The way that it'll typically work, too, is when that email is automatically sent out to people when they inquire, usually a few minutes later, an automated text message will go out as well.

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:20.000
judy: Right.

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.000
judy: Oh.

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:27.000
Whitney Hodges: And why that is important is because.

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Today. I mean, I'm sure it's like this for you. It's like this for me. Our inboxes are so chaotic, right? Like we're getting so many emails. The likelihood of somebody seeing a text and responding to a text is.

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:33.000
judy: Yeah.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
judy: No. Right.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:54.000
Whitney Hodges: so much higher than them seeing the email and responding to the email. But, you know, the purpose of that text can be, hey, just letting you know that we sent you some more information, it's in your inbox, go over there and check it out, sort of thing, right?

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.000
judy: Oh, okay.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:56.000
judy: Oh, okay, okay.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:25:10.000
Whitney Hodges: Or it could be, you know, there are a variety of different strategies. They could be, you know, we've sent you some more information. Would you like to schedule a tour? Or here is our link to schedule a tour. Or do you have a date in mind for your wedding? Right? Like, kind of just depending on if.

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:00.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.000
judy: Bye.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:11.000
judy: Right.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:30.000
Whitney Hodges: wanting to start that back and forth dial with that initially. Right? So part of that like nurture sequence that we're putting people in you know, if they've acquired, but not yet scheduled a tour can include more emails, more text messages. That's really just giving them more information on the venue kind of pre selling them on the venue.

00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:15.000
judy: Oh, okay.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:34.000
Whitney Hodges: encouraging them to get to that next step of scheduling.

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:36.000
judy: Okay. Okay.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:47.000
Whitney Hodges: And then, once they've scheduled a tour, which they can do, you know, through the… the LeadLock system as well, are you… are you currently using HoneyBook for scheduling tours, or Calendly, or what are you… what are you… you know?

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:48.000
judy: No, because we kinda, um…

00:25:48.000 --> 00:26:05.000
judy: we don't have, like, set days, you know, on doing tours, and, like, our office is not where the venue is. Uh, and so it's not like somebody's like, I want to come right now, we can't be like, no.

00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:08.000
judy: We weren't there. Yeah.

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:11.000
judy: And so, no, we do not, I mean…

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:14.000
judy: That's the thing, I feel like, um…

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:22.000
judy: Some of the things that we're doing are not what this generation likes or understands.

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh-huh.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:35.000
judy: And, uh… I mean, there's reasons we do it, but it's still not… because we're trying to make it a little more personable, like, when somebody's wanting information.

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:43.000
judy: Uh, saying, oh, hi, Whitney, you know, instead of, uh, just a hi.

00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:48.000
judy: But I think that's really not mattering anymore.

00:26:46.000 --> 00:27:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Well, just know that with the system, we can still personalize everything. You can still include everybody's name. It's not going to, it shouldn't feel generic. There's still the ability to like pop in, right, and have manual touch points where, you know, you're manually responding to a text or to an email, of course, if somebody has very specific questions.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:52.000
judy: Oh.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:57.000
judy: Okay, okay.

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:08.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:22.000
Whitney Hodges: But another thing I think that is important for today's couple is ease of booking, right? And so it's helpful for them if they're able to see a tour calendar of dates and times that would be available for them to come in, because oftentimes they're coordinating with.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:38.000
Whitney Hodges: their fiance, or maybe they're having, you know, parents, mom come, things like that. So being able to just kind of see that, and when they find a time that works for them, be able to book that and have it automatically be added to your calendar, um, I would say definitely is, you know, a best practice these days.

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
judy: Right.

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:36.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:39.000
judy: Okay.

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:56.000
Whitney Hodges: And then from there, the, you know, the system sends them, you know, email and text reminders about the tour. And they're not just reminders, right? Again, they're pre-selling them before the tour of, like, what information do you want somebody to know before they're even coming in?

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:48.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.000
judy: Right.

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:59.000
judy: Right, right, right. Mm-hmm.

00:27:56.000 --> 00:28:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Right? So that's kind of how the the system works, and we find that that really supports you with.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:05.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:22.000
Whitney Hodges: lead generation through ads, right? Because once you start running ads, your lead volume is going to increase, most definitely, right? So it's more to keep up with manual… if you're, you know, trying to do everything manually. Um, but also, too.

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:09.000
judy: Okay.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.000
judy: Okay. Uh-huh.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.000
judy: Right.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:35.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, for today's couples, I mean, we're all… we're all busy, right? There are lots of distractions, so we do often find that it can take several touch points after inquiry to turn that inquiry into a…

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:28.000
judy: Right.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:36.000
judy: ah…

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:41.000
Whitney Hodges: And so when you're just sending the one email, it can be money on the table.

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:37.000
judy: Gotcha.

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:39.000
judy: Right.

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:43.000
judy: Okay, okay, hmm.

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Yeah.

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:48.000
judy: Alright. Yeah, we… like I said, we just didn't want to take any, um…

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:55.000
judy: personalization away from the contact with people.

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:28:55.000 --> 00:29:02.000
judy: And the tours, it's going to be kind of hard because a lot of times people are like, well, I can't come.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:16.000
judy: this time, blah blah blah. You know, but uh… can you do one on this date? And so we'll be like, okay, can one of us be there for the tour? And then we do. So that's one thing that concerns me on that.

00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh-huh.

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:31.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Yeah. And so if you're not quite ready to have a tour calendar in place or use that piece of it, that's definitely OK. It's certainly not a requirement by any means.

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:18.000
judy: Yeah.

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.000
judy: Yeah.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.000
judy: Oh, yeah.

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.000
judy: Okay, alright.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:47.000
Whitney Hodges: And the whole purpose of the system, right, it's not to make things impersonal, it's not to replace any of the human sales conversations that do need to happen, right, to be able to couples, but it is meant to.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:38.000
judy: Right.

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:42.000
judy: Right.

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:44.000
judy: Right.

00:29:47.000 --> 00:30:05.000
Whitney Hodges: take some of the pressure off of… of you, right? Because you know that every lead is being responded to, um, when they initially inquire with an email and with a text message. You're gonna know that people who aren't, you know, ready to book a tour right away are still continuing to receive follow-up messages.

00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:58.000
judy: Uh-huh.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:06.000
judy: Right.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:20.000
Whitney Hodges: And then, you know, your warmest leads, or the leads that really kind of are the most responsive, you're able to still, you know, manually reply to their emails, reply to their text messages, and kind of have that sort of, um, back and forth dialogue. Mm-hmm.

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:16.000
judy: Right.

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:19.000
judy: Right.

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:27.000
judy: Okay, okay, alright. Okay, so then basically you can use that program.

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:22.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:33.000
judy: You can kind of have it conform to what you're needing it to do.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:36.000
Whitney Hodges: It's all totally customizable. Mm-hmm.

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:34.000
judy: Oh.

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:39.000
judy: Okay. Okay. That's good to hear. Okay. All right.

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, and I would say, you know, I mean, one of the best parts of it is that we set it all up for you, right? It's gonna be different than, like, you know, HoneyBook, probably you guys did the setup, you're doing connections on your own, you've kind of done that for yourself.

00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:46.000
judy: Okay, that's good.

00:30:51.000 --> 00:31:03.000
judy: Well, we were one of the first ones to sign with them, so we were, like, have a really good deal with them, you know, and yeah, and then we've been…

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, cool. Mm-hmm.

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:18.000
judy: beta testers a couple of times on stuff. So, uh… yeah, so, yeah, no, we… they… they kind of helped me set it all up and everything. Yeah, yeah. So, I… I just… yeah, but I don't want to get in…

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, nice! Okay.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:15.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, good. Okay. Okay.

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:33.000
judy: to, uh… I mean, I think we need to make it easier just to keep up with the change in generations. But, I mean, the thing is, if somebody's like, well, I don't want to do this, which we get from parents a lot, you know, with, um, payments.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Yep.

